            "command": "cd /home/leon0399/Projects/llame; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-leon0399-Projects-llame/4e288e6f-9d58-4b20-9659-ab38b7e6e217/scratchpad\nmk() { gh issue create --title \"$1\" --body-file \"$2\" --parent 701 | grep -o '[0-9]*$'; }\ncat > $S/f-order.md <<'EOF'\n## Outcome\n\nOrdering selectors for directory listings beyond the default directories-first, host-collation name order fixed by the `native-read-directory-listing` change: recency (OMP's mtime sort with newest-plus-oldest truncation) and a locale-free code-unit order for byte-identical output across hosts.\n\nParent: #701. Follows #704.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Selector grammar on a directory path, e.g. `:recent`, that changes ordering without changing bounds or rendering.\n- The default listing stays deterministic per the shipped requirement; selectors are opt-in.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nMetadata columns (separate issue). Filtering (separate issue).\nEOF\ncat > $S/f-meta.md <<'EOF'\n## Outcome\n\nPer-entry metadata in directory listings: file size, child count for directories, and modification time. The `native-read-directory-listing` change ships names and kinds only so unchanged directories render identically and prompt caches survive.\n\nParent: #701. Follows #704.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Decide which fields are default and which are selector-gated; mtime must render as an absolute UTC timestamp (OMP's prompt-cache argument), never a relative age.\n- Keep the deterministic-listing requirement: metadata changes only when the entry changes.\nEOF\ncat > $S/f-filter.md <<'EOF'\n## Outcome\n\nHidden-entry and ignore-file handling for directory listings. The `native-read-directory-listing` change lists entries verbatim: dotfiles, `.git`, `node_modules`, and everything `.gitignore` names appear by name.\n\nParent: #701. Follows #704.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Decide defaults (Gemini CLI hides and reports `(N ignored)`; OMP shows hidden but prunes `.git`, `node_modules`, and build outputs; OpenCode filters nothing).\n- Provide an opt-out selector so the model can see everything when it needs to.\n- Apply the same rule under `kb://` (#702), where a vault's `.obsidian` directory is the common case.\nEOF\ncat > $S/f-symlink.md <<'EOF'\n## Outcome\n\nOptionally descend symbolic links that point at directories. The `native-read-directory-listing` change lists every symbolic link as `name@` and never follows it.\n\nParent: #701. Follows #704.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Opt-in selector; realpath per link and a visited set to break cycles.\n- Following escapes the requested subtree, so `kb://` (#702) must keep containment: a link that resolves outside the Space is listed but not followed.\n- Root-target symlinks already resolve today; this issue is only about entries within a listing.\nEOF\nfor spec in \"feat(api): ordering selectors for directory listings|f-order\" \"feat(api): per-entry metadata in directory listings|f-meta\" \"feat(api): hidden and ignore filtering for directory listings|f-filter\" \"feat(api): follow symbolic links in directory listings|f-symlink\"; do echo \"${spec##*|} $(mk \"${spec%%|*}\" $S/${spec##*|}.md)\"; done\ncat > $S/c-702.md <<'EOF'\nDesign option recorded during the #704 grilling, for discovery when this issue is planned:\n\nA scheme layer in front of the native tools: a parser recognizes the `kb://` prefix, extracts the Space identifier, verifies the caller's access to that Space, and maps the remainder to the internal filesystem-native call (read, listing, edit, write) with the Space root as containment. The directory walker landing in `native-read-directory-listing` takes an injected `{ lstat, opendir }` port for this reason, so `kb://` reuses it under owner authorization rather than the Knowledge walker.\nEOF\ngh issue comment 702 --body-file $S/c-702.md >/dev/null && echo \"702 commented\"",
